---
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/review-lanes-dark.svg?raw';
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/review-lanes-light.svg?raw';
import Diagram from './Diagram.astro';
---

<Diagram
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  maxWidth={680}
  caption="Where review lives: UI changes merge on green CI alone; only the adapter boundaries and CI config ask for a second pair of eyes."
>
  A two-branch diagram starting from a pull request opened with a station-impact
  checklist declaring what the change touches. On the left, the fast lane for UI
  and flows covers screens, the station kit, copy, keyboard shortcuts, the pause
  guide, interactive training, and QA review UI -- self-merging on green CI in a
  median of six minutes with no human approval required. On the right, the
  contract lane for seams and gates covers order, media, inspection, and chat
  adapters, local mock parity with production rules, and CI workflow and browser
  benchmark gates -- requiring co-owner review and reviewed by commit on the branch.
</Diagram>
